---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="How this site is built" description="How mxsalata.com is built: static pages, no trackers or cookies, nothing at home open to the internet.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Colophon</p>
    <h1>How this site is built</h1>
    <p class="lead">Small, fast and private by design.</p>
  </div>
  <article class="paper">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Static pages at the edge</h2>
      <p>
        The site is plain HTML and CSS, built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and served by Cloudflare. Its
        <a href={`${SITE.github}/site`}>source is on GitHub</a>; each change goes through a pull request, and the build
        and its checks run before anything is published.
      </p>
      <h2>Nothing extra in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        No trackers, no analytics and no cookies. Every page loads only from this site: no fonts, scripts or images from
        elsewhere. The one script is the theme switch, which remembers your choice on your own device.
      </p>
      <h2>Light, Pastel and Dark</h2>
      <p>
        The themes come from <a href="/projects/aperture/">Aperture</a>, so the two read as one family. Auto follows your
        device's setting.
      </p>
      <h2>Nothing at home open to the internet</h2>
      <p>The servers that run at home take no connections from the internet; what friends need reaches them another way.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
